# Grothendieck Homage — Part 42 : laws of the arrow form under iterated pullback

Alexandre Grothendieck (1928-2014).

Phase 5 extension (#2159, EPIC #1646).

Parts 1-41 established the foundations: categories, sieves, topologies,
lattice laws, pullback identities, sheaf bases, covering closure,
calibration, subcanonicality, dense topologies, sheaves, internal hom,
Cech cohomology, Mayer-Vietoris limit, Kan extensions, adjunctions, monads,
equivalences, monoidal categories, limits and colimits, comma pairs, direct
images, proper theorems on the arrow form (`J.Covers S f`), on the bundled
cover (`J.Cover X`), the coherence laws of the pullback pseudo-functor
(Part 37), the functor laws of pullback (Part 38), the lattice laws of
topologies (Part 39), the laws of the arrow form under pullback (Part 40)
and the order laws of the arrow form (Part 41).

Part 42 establishes the **laws of the arrow form `J.Covers S f` under
iterated pullback of sieves**: Mathlib provides the topology axioms in
arrow form (`arrow_max`, `arrow_stable`, `arrow_trans`, `arrow_intersect`),
the definitional `covers_iff` and the laws of `Sieve.pullback`
(`pullback_id`, `pullback_comp`, `pullback_inter`), but **does not provide**
the reading of these laws in terms of `J.Covers`: the unit of pullback, its
associativity, the distributivity over meet and the commutation with sieve
generation along an arrow (conditioned by the existence of the pullbacks of
the family). This module states and proves them:

  - `covers_pullback_id` : pulling back by the identity is a neutral
    operation in arrow form (unit of the pullback pseudo-functor).
  - `covers_pullback_assoc` : pulling back along `g ≫ f` and then along
    `h` is pulling back along `g` then along `h` (associativity, coherence
    law of the pullback pseudo-functor).
  - `covers_sieve_pullback_inter` : the pullback of a meet sieve is the meet
    of the pullbacks (distributivity of pullback over the sieve lattice, in
    arrow form).
  - `covers_pullback_generate` : covering the sieve generated by
    `R.pullbackArrows f` is covering the sieve generated by `R` along the
    composite (generation / pullback commutation, in arrow form).

Each proof is a **genuine tactic proof** (DEEP vein): it composes the laws of
`Sieve.pullback` (`pullback_id`, `pullback_comp`, `pullback_inter`,
`pullbackArrows_comm`) with the definitional `covers_iff` and the arrow-form
law `covers_comp_iff` (Part 35). No proof is a re-export.

