import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Grothendieck
import Grothendieck.CoversArrow

namespace Grothendieck.PullbackCoversLaws_en

open CategoryTheory

/-!
## Section 1 : unit of pullback

`Sieve.pullback_id` identifies the pullback by the identity with the sieve
itself. In arrow form, pulling `S` back by `𝟙 X` therefore changes nothing:
`S.pullback (𝟙 X)` covers `f` exactly when `S` covers `f`. This is the unit
of the pullback pseudo-functor (the arrow-form counterpart of `pullbackId`
of Part 37, which stated it at the level of bundled covers `J.Cover X`).
-/

/-- Pulling the sieve back by the identity is a neutral operation in arrow
    form: `S.pullback (𝟙 X)` covers `f` if and only if `S` covers `f`.
    Proof: the definitional `covers_iff` reduces both sides to
    `S.pullback f ∈ J Y`, then `Sieve.pullback_id` identifies
    `S.pullback (𝟙 X)` with `S`. -/
theorem covers_pullback_id {C : Type*} [Category C] {X Y : C}
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (S : Sieve X) (f : Y ⟶ X) :
    J.Covers (S.pullback (𝟙 X)) f ↔ J.Covers S f := by
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff, GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff,
    Sieve.pullback_id]

/-!
## Section 2 : associativity of pullback

The law `Sieve.pullback_comp` says that pulling back along a composite
`g ≫ f` is pulling back along `g` of the sieve already pulled back by `f`.
In arrow form, this gives the associativity law of the pullback
pseudo-functor: `(S.pullback f).pullback g` and `S.pullback (g ≫ f)` cover
the same arrows.
-/

/-- The associativity law of pullback in arrow form: `(S.pullback f).pullback g`
    covers `h` if and only if `S.pullback (g ≫ f)` covers `h`. Proof: the
    definitional `covers_iff` reduces to the memberships, then
    `Sieve.pullback_comp` identifies the two pulled-back sieves. -/
theorem covers_pullback_assoc {C : Type*} [Category C] {W X Y Z : C}
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (S : Sieve Z) (f : Y ⟶ Z) (g : X ⟶ Y)
    (h : W ⟶ X) :
    J.Covers ((S.pullback f).pullback g) h ↔ J.Covers (S.pullback (g ≫ f)) h := by
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff, GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff,
    Sieve.pullback_comp]

/-!
## Section 3 : distributivity of pullback over meet

`Sieve.pullback_inter` pushes pullback into the meet of two sieves. In arrow
form, Part 41 read this law along a composite arrow (`covers_pullback_inter`:
`S ⊓ R` covers `g ≫ f`); here we read it on the pullback of the sieve itself:
`(S ⊓ R).pullback f` covers `g` if and only if `S.pullback f ⊓ R.pullback f`
covers `g`.
-/

/-- The distributivity of sieve pullback over meet, in arrow form:
    `(S ⊓ R).pullback f` covers `g` if and only if
    `S.pullback f ⊓ R.pullback f` covers `g`. Proof: `covers_iff` then
    `Sieve.pullback_inter`. -/
theorem covers_sieve_pullback_inter {C : Type*} [Category C] {X Y Z : C}
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (S R : Sieve X) (f : Y ⟶ X) (g : Z ⟶ Y) :
    J.Covers ((S ⊓ R).pullback f) g ↔ J.Covers (S.pullback f ⊓ R.pullback f) g := by
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff, GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff,
    Sieve.pullback_inter]

/-!
## Section 4 : generation / pullback commutation

The law `Sieve.pullbackArrows_comm` (Mathlib) relates the sieve generated by
the pullbacks of a family `R` of arrows to `X` with the pullback of the sieve
generated by `R`: `Sieve.generate (R.pullbackArrows f) = (Sieve.generate R).pullback f`,
conditional on the existence of the pullbacks of the arrows of `R` along `f`
(`R.HasPullbacks f`). In arrow form, composed with `covers_comp_iff`
(Part 35), this identity gives the generation / pullback commutation:
covering the sieve generated by the pullbacks of `R` along `f` is covering
the sieve generated by `R` along the composite `g ≫ f`.
-/

/-- The generation / pullback commutation in arrow form: covering the sieve
    generated by `R.pullbackArrows f` is covering the sieve generated by `R`
    along the composite. Proof: `Sieve.pullbackArrows_comm` replaces the
    sieve generated by the pullbacks with the pullback of the generated
    sieve, then `covers_comp_iff` (Part 35) gives its arrow-form reading. -/
theorem covers_pullback_generate {C : Type*} [Category C] {X Y Z : C}
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (R : Presieve X) (f : Y ⟶ X) (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    [R.HasPullbacks f] :
    J.Covers (Sieve.generate (R.pullbackArrows f)) g ↔
      J.Covers (Sieve.generate R) (g ≫ f) := by
  rw [Sieve.pullbackArrows_comm]
  exact Grothendieck.CoversArrow.covers_comp_iff J (Sieve.generate R) f g

end Grothendieck.PullbackCoversLaws_en
